WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.104
Module 6: the practical task.

00:00:02.104 --> 00:00:06.021
It has two written parts,
both from Northwind's world.

00:00:06.021 --> 00:00:10.736
In Part A, you'll plan a Culture
Dig for Northwind's six clinics.

00:00:10.736 --> 00:00:16.467
In Part B, you'll write the synthesis
memo that answers Alex's question: why do

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:18.063
decisions feel closed?

00:00:18.063 --> 00:00:19.877
Allow two to three hours.

00:00:19.877 --> 00:00:21.835
There's no video to record.

00:00:21.835 --> 00:00:26.478
This practical is task two of your
Mosaic Practitioner capstone.

00:00:26.478 --> 00:00:32.209
You'll hand it in on your capstone page
once you've finished all three courses.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:32.907
Dr.

00:00:32.907 --> 00:00:38.073
Chris Cancialosi scores your work
against ten criteria, five for each part,

00:00:38.073 --> 00:00:39.244
from one to four.

00:00:39.244 --> 00:00:42.826
To pass, you need at least
three on every criterion.

00:00:42.826 --> 00:00:48.062
Three things fail a submission outright:
identifying, or trying to identify,

00:00:48.062 --> 00:00:53.228
anyone in the evidence; planning to
report results for groups the dig can't

00:00:53.228 --> 00:00:57.223
support; and claiming the
evidence shows what caused what,

00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:00.392
or treating a score as
a grade or a benchmark.

00:01:00.392 --> 00:01:05.077
If you don't pass, you'll get written
feedback and one resubmission,

00:01:05.077 --> 00:01:09.141
and if that doesn't pass either,
a call to talk it through.

00:01:09.633 --> 00:01:11.833
It's June the fourteenth, 2027.

00:01:11.833 --> 00:01:15.735
Taylor Brooks, the vice
president of Clinic Operations,

00:01:15.735 --> 00:01:18.006
wants a dig for the six clinics.

00:01:18.006 --> 00:01:23.469
Taylor would like results for each
clinic, would like to be the Program Lead,

00:01:23.469 --> 00:01:27.514
and wants a report for the
board offsite in late October.

00:01:27.514 --> 00:01:31.771
Read the facts carefully: the
license, who holds which role,

00:01:31.771 --> 00:01:36.667
the size of each clinic, the
researchers who'd return, and the dates.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:40.285
You may recommend changes
to what Taylor asked for.

00:01:40.285 --> 00:01:41.633
If you do, say why.

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:43.423
Use this template.

00:01:43.423 --> 00:01:48.581
It covers your recommendation, the
license and waves, people and access,

00:01:48.581 --> 00:01:53.238
team staffing, the timeline, story
collection, protecting people,

00:01:53.238 --> 00:01:56.964
and a fieldwork plan for
two domains of your choice.

00:01:56.964 --> 00:02:01.621
Every decision you've practised
in this course has a place in it.

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:06.303
For Part B, Alex wants a two-page
memo for the executive team,

00:02:06.303 --> 00:02:08.725
ahead of a decision-rights workshop.

00:02:08.725 --> 00:02:13.634
Your evidence pack has the story
patterns, the report's "Where to start",

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:17.064
three team syntheses, some
anonymized observations,

00:02:17.064 --> 00:02:20.831
three story summaries and the
Culture Mosaic statements.

00:02:20.831 --> 00:02:25.875
Remember who will read it, including
the people whose decisions the stories

00:02:25.875 --> 00:02:26.480
describe.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.700
Write about patterns, not people.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.439
Open with a headline that
answers the question.

00:02:32.439 --> 00:02:37.400
Then give three findings, each with
a claim, evidence from both streams,

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.777
where they agree or diverge,
and your confidence.

00:02:40.777 --> 00:02:45.463
Say what it adds up to, what the
evidence can't tell the executives,

00:02:45.463 --> 00:02:48.426
and three or four
specific recommendations.

00:02:48.933 --> 00:02:50.350
Here's the full rubric.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:55.216
Read the descriptors for a three and a
four on each criterion before you start.

00:02:55.216 --> 00:02:58.912
They're the clearest guide to
what a strong submission does.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:03.994
The final exam has thirty questions,
open notes, in sixty minutes.

00:03:03.994 --> 00:03:08.101
You need eighty percent, and
every critical question right.

00:03:08.101 --> 00:03:10.398
Passing it completes this course.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:15.946
Before you hand it in, check that nothing
in either part points to an individual,

00:03:15.946 --> 00:03:19.622
and that you haven't promised
anything a dig can't deliver.

00:03:19.622 --> 00:03:19.808
Dr.

00:03:19.808 --> 00:03:23.671
Chris Cancialosi will score it
with the rest of your capstone.

00:03:23.671 --> 00:03:26.225
When all four capstone tasks have passed,

00:03:26.225 --> 00:03:29.465
you're Mosaic Practitioner
Certified for five years.

00:03:29.465 --> 00:03:31.956
Thank you for doing this work carefully.

00:03:31.956 --> 00:03:35.507
The people who tell you their
stories are counting on it.

